"""The two IPSec finding models, and the two control types they answer to. PAN-IPS-001 to 009.

PHASE 2 OF THE TUNNEL, NOT PHASE 1. `IkeCryptoProfileFinding` and `IkeGatewayFinding` already
exist over the objects at the ADJACENT xpath, and the four class names across the two phases are
near-identical. These two are over `integrations.IpsecCryptoProfile` and
`integrations.IpsecTunnel`, built by migration `integrations.0114_ipsec_crypto`.

THE `AlterField` ON `control_type` IS THE ENUM AND WAS GENERATED, NEVER HAND-WRITTEN. The
choices list is a literal that must match `Control.ControlType` exactly, and
`makemigrations --check --dry-run` is the only thing that catches a transcription slip. Two
members are added here: `ipsec_crypto_profile` (20 characters) and `ipsec_tunnel` (12), against
a `max_length` of 64 - measured before the enum line was written, because the field is a BOUND
and not a registration: at the old width of 32 a 34-character value made `makemigrations` refuse
outright with `fields.E009` and generate nothing.

TWO TYPES FOR THREE STAGE 5 SUBJECTS, AND THE THIRD GETS NOTHING. `monitor-profile` is named by
no stage 5 assertion - it appears only in PAN-IPS-007's second record, which is discharged to
`engineer_answers` - so there is no verdict to grade and no finding to generate. Its model
exists and is normalised; what is missing is not configuration. A type minted for it would be a
search surface no control asks for.

NINE CONTROLS AND TWO FINDING MODELS, with PAN-IPS-009 split across them. Its two assertion
records name different subjects - a tunnel running on a crypto profile nobody chose, and a
profile no tunnel names - and `Control._CONTROL_TYPE_TARGET_MODEL` is one-to-one while
`ControlQuery.clean()` refuses a query on any other model. So the control ships as the PROFILE
half and is silent about the tunnel half. The column that would answer the tunnel side,
`IpsecTunnel.effective_crypto_profile_chosen`, is registered in the compiler and carries no
query. The stage 8 artifact for `ipsec-crypto` records the choice and the grounds.
"""

